  "name": "Activities of advertising, market research and public relations",
  "section": "N",
  "summary": "Agencies, ad-tech, out-of-home, market-research and PR firms describe AI in creative production, media planning and bidding, audience modelling, synthetic respondents and media monitoring, usually through named in-house AI platforms. The dominant risk theme is disintermediation: platform-native AI ad tools, clients in-housing, AI search eroding traffic and search advertising, and pressure on FTE-based fees and headcount. Filings also cover copyright in AI-generated work, likeness and digital-replica rights, brand safety against AI-generated content and ad fraud, and labelling and provenance rules.",
